            <ArticleTitle>[Rotational atherectomy in a patient with non-ST elevation acute coronary syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>854-7; discussion 858</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Rotational atherectomy is a valuable technique complementary to PCI in complex calcified coronary artery stenoses. A case of a 65 year-old man with non-ST elevation acute myocardial infarction (NSTEMI) treated with PCI with rotational atherectomy followed by two drug eluting stents (DES) implantation is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
